  "description_html": "Scale diagram of crocodyliforms 10 metres (32.8 ft) or more in length, based on recent size estimates by 2015.\n<ul><li><i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Purussaurus\" title=\"Category:Purussaurus\">Purussaurus</a> brasiliensis</i>: body length of 12.5 m according to Aureliano et al. (2015),<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> skull shape according to Aguilera et al. (2006)<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<ul><li><i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Sarcosuchus\" title=\"Category:Sarcosuchus\">Sarcosuchus</a> imperator</i>: body length of 11–12 m and skull shape according to Sereno et al. (2001)<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<ul><li><i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Deinosuchus\" title=\"Category:Deinosuchus\">Deinosuchus</a> riograndensis</i>: body length of 10.6 m according to Farlow et al. (2005),<sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> skull shape according to Schwimmer (2002)<sup id=\"cite_ref-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<ul><li><i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Gryposuchus\" title=\"Category:Gryposuchus\">Gryposuchus</a> croizati</i>: body length of 10.15 m and skull shape according to Riff &amp; Aguilera (2008)<sup id=\"cite_ref-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<ul><li><i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Euthecodon\" title=\"Category:Euthecodon\">Euthecodon</a> brumpti</i>: body length of 10 m and skull shape according to Storrs (2003)<sup id=\"cite_ref-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<ul><li><i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodylus_porosus\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Crocodylus porosus\">Crocodylus</a> porosus</i>: body length of 6.3 meters according to Britton et al. (2012)<sup id=\"cite_ref-Britton_et_al._2012_8-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Britton_et_al._2012-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>",
